  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Culture and Development East Africa-Artistic rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Sanaa rights&quot; (artistic rights) is a project that seeks to strengthen cultural rights through enhancing the policy and legislative landscape for the Tanzanian cultural sector.The project also seeks to strengthen gender equality in the sector. The implementing partner is Culture and development in East Africa (CDEA), a Tanzanian NGO based in Dar es Salaam. Their cooperating partner is Tanzania Artists Rights Organizations (TARO).

Impact: Enhanced policy and legislative framewkr for Tanzania art sector

Outcome 1: Enhanced policy knowledge for improving the status of the artists in Tanzania
Outcome 2: CDEA&apos;s organizational capacity enhanced
Outcome 3: Improved knowledge on the need for harmonized legal framework for the Tanzanian arts sector

Support period: 7 Dec 2022-31 Dec 2025</narrative>
  </description>
